-- title:
--   Hecke relations on J₀(N) hold on S₂(Γ₀(N))
-- statement:
--   Let $N$ be a non-zero natural number. Assume [`ModularCurve.HeckeInputsAll N`](def/ModularCurve_HeckeInputsAll.html#L8): for every prime $\ell$ the predicate `HeckeInputsAlong` holds for the base field $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, level $N$ and $\ell$, that is, there are integrality data for the two maps $\alpha,\beta$ at $\ell$ (`HeckeAlphaBarIntegral`, `HeckeBetaBarIntegral`), all divisors of degree zero on the base-changed modular function field of level $N\ell$ are principal, $\alpha$ is finite along $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, and the fundamental identity for $\beta$ together with the norm formula for $\alpha$ hold. Assume further [`ModularCurve.HeckeOperatorsCommuteBar N`](def/ModularCurve_HeckeModule.html#L25): the endomorphisms `heckeOperatorBar N ℓ` of $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ commute pairwise as $\ell$ runs over the primes. Let $t$ be an element of [`ModularCurve.HeckeAlg`](def/HeckeGalois_EichlerShimura.html#L14), the polynomial ring $\mathbb Z[X_\ell : \ell \text{ prime}]$ in variables indexed by `Nat.Primes`, and suppose that $t$ annihilates every element of [`ModularCurve.JZero N`](def/ModularCurve_ArithmeticGalois.html#L115) for the module structure `heckeModuleBar N`, which under the commutation hypothesis is the action in which $X_\ell$ acts by `heckeOperatorBar N ℓ` on the group $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of degree-zero divisor classes, modulo principal divisors, of the base change `modularFunctionFieldBar N` of the full modular function field of level $N$ to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$. The conclusion is that $t$ also evaluates to zero in the commutative ring $\mathbb T =$ [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 ∅`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18), the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb C} S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell \nmid N$ and $U_q$ for primes $q \mid N$, the evaluation sending the variable at a prime $\ell$ to [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra.U`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L80) at $\ell$ when $\ell \mid N$ and to [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra.T`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L77) at $\ell$ otherwise.
--
--   This is the faithfulness direction of Eichler–Shimura theory in the form needed here: the analytic weight-two Hecke algebra of level $N$, with the operators $U_q$ at the primes dividing $N$ included, is a quotient of the abstract polynomial Hecke algebra acting on the Jacobian $J_0(N)$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, so every relation valid on divisor classes is valid on cusp forms. It is used to transfer eigenform data between the two modules, in [`ModularCurve.eigenformSupportAt_jZero`](thm.html#ModularCurve.eigenformSupportAt_jZero) and in the identification of the kernels of the two evaluation maps, [`ModularCurve.ker_heckeEvalForms_latticeRestrict_eq_ker_heckeEvalBar`](thm.html#ModularCurve.ker_heckeEvalForms_latticeRestrict_eq_ker_heckeEvalBar).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_aeval_heckeAlgebra_eq_zero_of_forall_smul_jZero_eq_zero.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_HeckeModule
import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_HeckeInputsAll
import Definitions.Def_CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

theorem ModularCurve.aeval_heckeAlgebra_eq_zero_of_forall_smul_jZero_eq_zero (N : ℕ) [NeZero N]
    (hin : ModularCurve.HeckeInputsAll N) (hcomm : ModularCurve.HeckeOperatorsCommuteBar N)
    (t : ModularCurve.HeckeAlg)
    (ht : letI := ModularCurve.heckeModuleBar N; ∀ x : ModularCurve.JZero N, t • x = 0) :
    MvPolynomial.aeval (R := ℤ)
      (fun ℓ : Nat.Primes => if h : (ℓ : ℕ) ∣ N
        then (CuspForm.heckeAlgebra.U (S := (∅ : Set ℕ)) ℓ.prop h (Set.notMem_empty _) :
          CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 (∅ : Set ℕ))
        else CuspForm.heckeAlgebra.T (S := (∅ : Set ℕ)) ℓ.prop h (Set.notMem_empty _)) t = 0 := by sorry
